\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O thou, whom once they flocked to hear,
\par Thy words to hear, Thy power to feel;
\par Suffer the sinners to draw near,
\par And graciously receive us still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. They that be whole, Thyself hast said,
\par No need of a physician have;
\par But I am sick, and want Thine aid;
\par And want Thine utmost power to save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy power, and truth, and love divine,
\par The same from age to age endure;
\par A word, a gracious word of Thine,
\par The most inveterate plague can cure.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Helpless howe'er my spirits lies,
\par And long hath languished at the pool,
\par A word of Thine shall make me rise,
\par And speak me in a moment whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Make this the acceptable hour;
\par Come, O my soul's physician Thou!
\par Display Thy sanctifying power,
\par And show me Thy salvation now.
\par                                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

